        	<h1>Problems of Existing Recruiting process without Tools.</h1>
            <h3><i class="fa fa-calendar-check-o"></i>Posted On : <span>12 DEC 2016 at 11:05 AM</span></h3>
            <div class="blogImg"><img src="/resources/static-web/images/bl3.jpg" alt=""/></div>
            <p>As the current business process is not automated the company needs to cope up with the following set of problems.
            </p>
            <b>Performance: </b>
            <p>Response time: Delay in the resource submission to the client manually with using excels.<br>
            Poor time management: Often paperwork is more, which results in delay on client’s services.<br>
            Follow-up resources frequently are missing.</p>
			<b>Information: </b>
         	<p>Redundant information: Information about resources stored in many places.<br>
         	Data is captured redundantly: Information has to be captured again and again when the requirement is new. Not storing the resource previous which has collected for the same requirement.<br>
         	Duplicity: Due to lack of store resources in a single source, large duplicates occur.<br>
         	Due to a large number of manual files, data organization is difficult and is not easy to meet new information needs from stored data.</p>
			<b>Economics:</b>
			<p>Manual handling of data is expensive as compared to an automated system. The cost in terms of time is high. 
         	</p>
			<b>Control (and security): too little security  </b>
         <p>Difficulty in keeping track of resource hiring and activities. <br>
         Decision-making slow due to lack of credibility of reports. [While interview schedule of resource who are flexible for respective date]</p>
			<b>Efficiency </b>
         <p>Inefficiency due to lack of proper communication between the team.<br>
         Effort and materials required for tasks are excessive.</p>
			<b>Services</b>
         <p>Follow up the resource is very poor.<br>
         Inconsistency in decision making while rating employees.</p>
